# DirectX12 Backend Rules

- Never expose DirectX12 types outside backend layer.
- Never expose ComPtr outside DX12 implementation.
- Use PImpl for DX12-facing classes when beneficial.
- Encapsulate descriptor heap management.
- Encapsulate resource state transitions.
- Prefer RAII for GPU resource lifetime.
- Validate resource states carefully.
- Minimize CPU/GPU synchronization.
- Avoid redundant resource barriers.
- Prefer explicit state tracking.
- Keep command list lifecycle clear and predictable.
- Separate upload resources from GPU-only resources.
- Avoid hidden synchronization.
- Use descriptive debug names for GPU resources.
- Prefer fence-based synchronization abstractions.
- Keep backend implementation isolated from gameplay systems.